# NightFalcon (Cursor port)

This repo contains the NightFalcon adversarial security-review pipeline for
Cursor. It is driven by the `/nightfalcon` skill
(`.cursor/skills/nightfalcon/SKILL.md`), NOT by ad-hoc analysis.

- Run a review with `/nightfalcon <repo-url…>` (or `/nightfalcon --triage
  <findings-file>`). The skill is the orchestrator; it spawns one
  context-isolated subagent per phase and enforces order with shell gates.
- **Never bypass the gate scripts.** `scripts/check-gate.sh` runs before every
  phase and `scripts/complete-phase.sh` after; exit 2 = BLOCKED. `state.json`
  is the source of truth for `current_phase` / `repo_slugs` / `phase_status`.
- **Hooks** (`.cursor/hooks.json`): `beforeShellExecution` (gate-guard, blocks
  shell tampering with review state), `afterFileEdit` (edit-log, advisory
  only — Cursor cannot block edits), `stop` (stop-enforce, nudges phase
  completion via `followup_message`). All are no-ops outside a workspace with
  both `.nightfalcon-review` and canonical `state.json`; nested working
  directories resolve back to that initialized workspace.
- **Workspace is always `$PWD`.** Artifacts land under `findings/<slug>/`,
  `output/`, and PoCs under `output/proof_of_concept/<slug>/`. Cloned source is
  `sourcecode/<slug>/` (gitignored).
- **Enums are authoritative** (`references/enums.md`): tiers `P0..P4` (the
  report also shows the severity word, e.g. `P0 (Critical)`); dispositions
  `CONFIRMED | CONFIRMED-MODIFIED | DISMISSED | NEEDS-REVIEW`; exposure
  `EXTERNAL | INTERNAL | INTERNAL-RESTRICTED` (§17); PoC verdicts `VALID |
  NEEDS-REVISION | INVALID`.
- **PoCs are self-contained**: each script declares its parameters inline
  (prefilled where safe, blank `# FILL:` otherwise) and does NOT source a
  shared config to run. One per-repo `POC-GUIDE-<DATE>.md` documents every
  PoC's parameters; `poc-config.env` is a reference catalog only. PoCs cover
  P0/P1/P2 only — never Low (P3) / Informational (P4).
- **Model**: never selected or switched by the plugin; omit the `model`
  argument and every reasoning override so every spawn uses the user's
  currently-selected Cursor model, never downgraded.

See `README.md` for install and `references/context-scope.md` for what each
phase reads and writes.
